---
import LibraryLayout from "../../layouts/LibraryLayout.astro";
import "../../styles/section-pages.css";
---
<LibraryLayout activeSection="about" title="About Ridwanah — Digital Health Education" description="Learn about Ridwanah's purpose, approach and commitment to accessible, source-led health education.">
  <div id="top" class="policy-page">
    <div class="library-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>About Ridwanah</span></div>
    <section class="policy-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> WHY RIDWANAH EXISTS</div>
      <h1>Health knowledge<br /><em>should be within reach.</em></h1>
      <p>Ridwanah is a digital health education project built around a simple idea: people deserve clear, responsible information that helps them understand health topics and ask better questions.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="policy-content">
      <section><h2>Our purpose</h2><p>We aim to make public-health information easier to access, understand and use in everyday conversations. The platform brings together plain-language learning guides, selected health news, video resources and awareness information.</p></section>
      <section><h2>What Ridwanah is</h2><p>Ridwanah is an educational platform. It is not a hospital, clinic, emergency service, diagnostic tool or substitute for a qualified healthcare professional. We do not provide individual diagnosis or treatment through the website.</p></section>
      <section><h2>How we approach health information</h2><ul><li>Start with reputable sources, especially primary public-health organisations.</li><li>Explain information in accessible language without changing the meaning of the source.</li><li>Show source links, publication dates and review status.</li><li>Make uncertainty and limitations visible rather than presenting guesses as facts.</li><li>Correct or remove content when reliable evidence shows it is inaccurate or out of date.</li></ul></section>
      <section><h2>Respect for people</h2><p>Health topics can be personal. Ridwanah aims to use respectful language, avoid stigma and recognise that health experiences are shaped by people’s circumstances, communities and access to care.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Our current stage</h2><p>The website is being developed as a static educational resource. Some sections are curated drafts and some external resources are maintained by their original publishers. Medical review is not claimed unless a qualified reviewer and the review details are genuinely confirmed.</p></section>
      <div class="policy-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/health">Explore the health library <span>↗</span></a><a class="policy-text-link" href="/editorial-policy">Read our editorial policy <span>→</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</LibraryLayout>
